{"parentUuid":"f5c84a31-65df-4959-91fb-ea0918bf06a1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a3302efe-2781-4033-8f98-81028d0ab45f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KrJK7bLdTAYytfB9gykjJe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: changelog\n3\tdescription: >\n4\t  Generate or update the CHANGELOG.md for a new release version.\n5\t  Use when the user says \"generate changelog\", \"update changelog\", \"write release notes\",\n6\t  or asks to prepare a changelog for a version like \"changelog for 0.5.3\".\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t# Changelog Generation\n10\t\n11\tGenerate a changelog entry for a new release by analyzing merged PRs since the last tag.\n12\t\n13\t## Parameters\n14\t\n15\tThe user provides:\n16\t- **Version number** -- e.g., `0.5.3`\n17\t- **Additional PRs** -- optionally, PRs not yet merged that should be included\n18\t\n19\t## Step 1: Gather Data\n20\t\n21\t1. Find the previous release tag: `git tag --sort=-version:refname | head -1`\n22\t2. List all merge commits since that tag: `git log <tag>..HEAD --merges --format='%s' | grep -v \"Merge branch\"`\n23\t3. Get PR details with: `gh pr list --state merged --base main --search \"merged:><tag-date>\" --json number,title,author --limit 50`\n24\t4. List contributors: `git log <tag>..HEAD --format='%an' --no-merges | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn`\n25\t\n26\t## Step 2: Identify External Contributors\n27\t\n28\tTo determine if a contributor is external, check for an `@entire.io` email:\n29\t\n30\t```bash\n31\tgit log --all --format='%an <%ae>' --author=\"<name>\" | sort -u\n32\t```\n33\t\n34\tIf they have an `@entire.io` email anywhere in git history, they are **internal**. Only list external contributors in the Thanks section.\n35\t\n36\tAlso check the memory file at `memory/project_team_members.md` for known internal/external mappings.\n37\t\n38\t## Step 3: Write the Entry\n39\t\n40\tInsert the new version section at the top of `CHANGELOG.md`, after the header and before the previous version.\n41\t\n42\t### Format\n43\t\n44\tFollow the existing style in CHANGELOG.md exactly:\n45\t\n46\t```markdown\n47\t## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD\n48\t\n49\t### Added\n50\t\n51\t- Feature description with context ([#123](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/123))\n52\t\n53\t### Changed\n54\t\n55\t- Change description ([#456](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/456))\n56\t\n57\t### Fixed\n58\t\n59\t- Bug fix description ([#789](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/789))\n60\t\n61\t### Housekeeping\n62\t\n63\t- Maintenance item ([#101](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/101))\n64\t\n65\t### Thanks\n66\t\n67\tThanks to @contributor for description of contribution!\n68\t```\n69\t\n70\t### Style Rules\n71\t\n72\t- **Sections**: Added, Changed, Fixed, Housekeeping, Thanks. Omit empty sections.\n73\t- **Each bullet**: starts with a dash, concise description, PR link(s) at the end\n74\t- **Group related PRs** into a single bullet when they're part of the same feature/fix\n75\t- **Work-in-progress features**: call out explicitly, e.g., \"Feature X (work in progress): ...\"\n76\t- **Known limitations**: note inline, e.g., \"Note: subagent tracking is not yet supported due to...\"\n77\t- **Thanks section**: only external contributors. Name what they contributed specifically.\n78\t- **Dependency bumps**: group into a single Housekeeping bullet unless a bump fixes a notable bug\n79\t- **PR links**: always use full URL format `[#N](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/N)`\n80\t- **No trailing period** on bullet items\n81\t- **Date**: use the current date in YYYY-MM-DD format\n82\t\n83\t### Categorization Guide\n84\t\n85\t- **Added**: new features, new commands, new agent integrations, new CI workflows\n86\t- **Changed**: behavior changes, API changes, UX changes, migrations\n87\t- **Fixed**: bug fixes, E2E fixes, agent-specific fixes\n88\t- **Housekeeping**: dependency bumps, docs, refactors, CI improvements, test improvements\n89\t"}]},"uuid":"95084790-c388-4305-9343-aff