.go` are renamed copies of the old tour tests. `Generate(..., Regenerate: true)`, `regenerateFromAgent`, `translateLearnError`, `cachedLearnSettingsLoader`, `executeLearn`, and the spinner cancel flow (`errLearnCancelled`) have zero coverage. Particularly notable: the just-added `Skipping ResolveState here also lets --regenerate succeed in CI checkouts that have no .entire/settings.json` (`run.go:73-78`) is a behavior the regen pipeline depends on, untested. At minimum add a stub-Generator test asserting `Generate(ctx, root, Options{Regenerate: true})` returns workflow-stage prompt + stripped output without calling `LoadSettings`/`ListInstalledAgents`.\n\n4. **`learn.yml` `paths` filter misses two breakage modes the workflow exists to catch.** `.github/workflows/learn.yml:5-7` triggers only on `embedded/learn.md` or `learn.yml` changes. (a) A PR that renames/moves `embedded/learn.md` to a different path will not trigger and will produce a binary with no embedded markdown — `//go:embed` would fail at build time, but no learn.yml gate. (b) A PR that modifies the `//go:embed` directive in `embedded.go` to point at a different filename won't trigger. Fix: also include `cmd/entire/cli/learn/embedded.go` in the paths filter, or just run the check on all PRs (it's a 4-line grep).\n\n5. **`mise-tasks/learn/regenerate` traps `EXIT` and unconditionally `rm -f \"$tmp\"`, but on success the final `mv \"$tmp\" \"$target\"` makes `$tmp` not exist — so the trap is a no-op there. Good.** However the trap runs even after success and silently swallows the case where the mv failed (e.g., target on read-only filesystem). `set -e` should catch a failed mv, but the trap fires before the user sees a clear error. Low severity but if you want maximum signal, clear the trap on success: `trap - EXIT`.\n\n**Low**\n\n6. **`entire/cli/learn/run.go:137` returns `\"generate tour with %s\"` — user-visible string still says \"tour\".** Cosmetic; matches the comment-level \"tour\" usage elsewhere whe